data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-summary.md\", \"content\": \"# Dispatch d002 — summary\\n\\n## What I implemented\\n\\n- `src/greet.py`: a `greet(name)` function that returns `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`.\\n- `tests/test_greet.py`: `unittest.TestCase` with two tests:\\n  - `test_normal_name`: `greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`\\n  - `test_empty_string`: `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n\\n  The test file inserts `../src` onto `sys.path` so `greet` is importable\\n  when running via `unittest discover` from the repo root (there's no\\n  package/install setup in this repo yet).\\n\\n## Test run\\n\\nCommand (from `~/subject` repo root):\\n\\n```\\npython3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n```\\n\\nOutput:\\n\\n```\\n..\\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\\nRan 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\nOK\\n```\\n\\nExit code: `0`.\\n\\n## Commit\\n\\nCommitted to my own branch `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`:\\n\\n```\\nf05ce88 Add greet function with unit tests\\n 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+)\\n create mode 100644 src/greet.py\\n create mode 100644 tests/test_greet.py\\n```\\n\\n`git status` is clean aside from untracked `__pycache__/` directories\\ngenerated by the test run (not committed, harmless).\\n\\n## Notes / caveats\\n\\nNone — the dispatch was implemented exactly as specified, no blockers.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

